`ValidateBlock()` can crash on a coin with an impossible confirmation height.

Validation assumes every spent coin was created in an earlier block. The UTXO set guarantees that, but coins from the callback don't. For example, say a block at height 1 spends a coin the callback reports as confirmed at height 100. If the spending transaction uses a time-based relative lock (BIP68), the lock check looks up block 99 among the block's ancestors. That block doesn't exist, so the lookup returns null and an assertion stops the process, even in release builds.

The suggested fix below treats a fetched coin as missing if its height isn't below the block's height, so validation returns `INVALID` instead of crashing. That includes coins at the block's own height: the block's own outputs are never fetched, so a coin claiming that height can't be genuine.

The test checks that a coin from an earlier height is still accepted, and that coins at the block's height or far in the future are rejected.

